> > but they only specify a formula to determine hit points if the
> > HD is >50.

Those aren't HD, they're an encoding of HP into the same field.
 
>   HD are d8.

In most cases. This being NetHack, there are exceptions. See the
part of makemon() that sets mtmp->mhpmax; in summary:

level 0 monsters have d4 HP
elementals on their own plane have their HP tripled
Riders have a fixed 10d8 regardless of level
adult dragons in the Endgame always roll 8 on their hit dice, and
  elsewhere have hit dice of 4+d4
golems have fixed HP values regardless of level, listed in golemhp()

